cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Dyne: physical models split across cooperating microcontrollers"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Dyne runs a physical model split across many microcontrollers. Each device
  computes the physics of its own patch of space and exchanges only the values
  at the borders with its neighbours, so the patches together form one
  simulation of the whole space without a central server doing the computation.
  Numerical models are compiled once to WebAssembly, and a solution split over
  N devices matches the single-device solution bit for bit. A deterministic
  network simulator (packet loss, delay, pauses, partitions) makes every run
  reproducible. Dyne is the first toolchain of the Physical-Edge Native
  Architecture project.
authors:
  - family-names: "Koyabu"
    given-names: "Natsuhi"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24241009"
